In Delphine's practice, the concept operates as an originary force, an immanent logic that precedes and determines its own conditions of material instantiation. The medium does not pre-exist the work but is called forth by the idea itself, such that photography, video art and film emerge not as discrete disciplinary choices but as contingent modalities through which thought achieves its sensible form. The artwork, in this sense, is less an object than an event of mediation between concept and matter.

